* ======================================================================
* SrvrAccount  -  Logto named account
* In:  account name

vb.account:
* Run the ON.LOGTO paragraph, if it exists

readv i from @voc,'ON.LOGTO',0 on error null
then execute 'ON.LOGTO' trapping aborts capturing response

new.account = upcase(cmnd)

old.account.path = account.path

if len(new.account) < 1 or len(new.account) > MAX.ACCOUNT.NAME.LEN then
   server.error = SV$ERROR
   error.msg = sysmsg(5037) ;* Invalid account name
   goto revert.to.old.account
end

* 13 Aug 26 Windows port - this took an account name or a pathname, and a
*   pathname reached a directory without going through the register at all.
*   Accounts are reached by name, as they are at LOGTO.  See PROJECT_STATUS.md
*   section 5.6.

* 17 Aug 26 Windows port - acc.group is read HERE, inside the block where
*   acc.rec is known to be assigned, and initialised to '' beside account.path
*   above it.  Reading it after the close would be reachable with acc.rec
*   never set - an unassigned reference is a compile-time WARNING and a
*   run-time abort in a program that may not run until much later, which is
*   the ERRGEN trap in PROJECT_STATUS.md section 6 and what bootstrap.py
*   line 229 refuses a build for.

account.path = ''
acc.group = ''
openpath @sdsys:@ds:'accounts' to acc.f then
   read acc.rec from acc.f, new.account then
      account.path = parse.pathname.tokens(acc.rec<ACC$PATH>)
      acc.group = acc.rec<ACC$GROUP>
   end
   close acc.f
end

if account.path = '' then
   server.error = SV$ERROR
   error.msg = sysmsg(10003) ;* User not allowed in requested account
   goto revert.to.old.account
end

* rev 0.9.0 * is user member of account?
* 13 Aug 26 Windows port - removed.  ACC$GROUP named a linux group.  Nothing
*   has replaced it here: the API server has no credential model yet, so any
*   session it accepts can still reach any account by name.  The LOGTO grant
*   check in CPROC does not apply to this path.  See PROJECT_STATUS.md 5.6.
* 17 Aug 26 Windows port - AND NOW IT IS BACK, section 7 step 6c.  The comment
*   above is left standing because its reason was right: the check waited on a
*   credential model, and step 6a built one.  Entry to an account is membership
*   of the Windows group named in its ACC$GROUP, which CREATE.ACCOUNT writes as
*   sdu_<name> - the same rule CPROC's logto.authorised applies at LOGTO, and
*   the operating system rather than SD records the grant.
*
*   ONLY THE GROUP TEST TRANSFERS from logto.authorised, and its other three
*   gates do not apply here: K$INTERNAL is set only by "sd -internal" or
*   "sd -I", which an API session never has, and elev.obtained is a CPROC
*   local with no meaning in this program.
*
* 20 Aug 26 Windows port - THIS USED TO SAY K$ADMINISTRATOR DESCRIBES "SESSION
*   STATE AN API SESSION CANNOT HAVE", AND THAT IS FALSE ON WINDOWS.  sdwind
*   is a service running as LocalSystem and accept_api_session() fork()s the
*   session, so it inherits the SERVICE's token, not the connecting client's.
*   kernel.c seeds USR_ADMIN from IsElevated() with no test of connection
*   type, and LocalSystem's token carries BUILTIN\Administrators.
*
*   MEASURED, not deduced - gplbld/verify-apiadmin.ps1, 20 Aug 2026: a
*   PROGRAMMER-tier account over a remote API connection OPENED AND WROTE
*   $cred, which is granted to SYSTEM and Administrators and to nothing else.
*
*   DO NOT REASON FROM THAT SENTENCE.  It was written when this port assumed
*   an API session ran as the connecting user, which it does on Linux and does
*   not here.  PROJECT_STATUS.md's opening section carries the finding and the
*   fix options; nothing is fixed yet.
*
*   BEWARE THE TWO "INTERNAL"S WHILE READING THAT ROUTINE, because they are
*   different things with almost the same name and both are in play in this
*   file.  K$INTERNAL reads internal_mode (op_kernel.c:140), a SESSION flag
*   set only by "sd -internal" or "sd -I" (sd.c:338, sd.c:349) - both behind
*   check_admin(), so it already implies elevation, and an API session, which
*   is spawned with -C/-N/-Q, never has it.  The $internal on line 64 of this
*   program is a different flag entirely: HDR_INTERNAL in the program header,
*   which is what BCOMP checks to allow KERNEL at all and what gates
*   K$SET.USERNAME above (op_kernel.c).  A program can be $internal in a
*   session that is not internal_mode, which is exactly this one.
*
*   THE IDENTITY IS kernel(K$USERNAME,0), NOT the local logname, which holds
*   the same value today by both routes above.  K$USERNAME reads
*   process.username - what K$SET.USERNAME wrote after the SCRAM proof
*   check in vb.scram.final (it was !CRED_VERIFY until phase 5), and what
*   audit_message() stamps every record with in C (section 7 step 4).  A grant
*   check able to disagree with the audit trail about who acted would make the
*   trail worthless, so the two read one source deliberately.
*
*   AN ACCOUNT WITH NO ACC$GROUP IS REFUSED rather than having sdu_<name>
*   guessed for it.  That is the rule section 7 step 5a sets for GRANT: an
*   empty field means a record older than CREATE.ACCOUNT's group work, and
*   inventing the name would test a group nothing else uses.
*
*   AND IT REFUSES SDSYS THROUGH THE API, which is intended and not a side
*   effect to be fixed later.  ACCOUNTS/SDSYS carries ACC$GROUP = sdsys, which
*   is not a Windows group and never has been (section 6), so is_grp_member
*   answers false with status 1.
*
* 20 Aug 26 Windows port - THE SECOND HALF OF THIS IS DELETED, and it said
*   "Administration needs elevation and an API session cannot have it, so
*   there is nothing to admit."  An API session runs as LocalSystem - see the
*   note above.  THE REFUSAL STILL HOLDS, and for the reason above it rather
*   than for that one: ACC$GROUP names no Windows group, so the group test
*   fails.  What is gone is the belief that it would not matter if it passed.
*
*   THE REFUSAL REUSES sysmsg(10003), the message the missing-account branch
*   above already gives.  A caller therefore cannot tell "no such account" from
*   "not granted", so the API does not enumerate accounts for an attacker.
deffun is_grp_member(user,group) calling '!is_grp_member'

if acc.group = '' then
   server.error = SV$ERROR
   error.msg = sysmsg(10003) ;* User not allowed in requested account
   goto revert.to.old.account
end

if not(is_grp_member(kernel(K$USERNAME, 0), acc.group)) then
   server.error = SV$ERROR
   error.msg = sysmsg(10003) ;* User not allowed in requested account
   goto revert.to.old.account
end

if not(ospath(account.path, OS$CD)) then
   server.error = SV$ERROR
   error.msg = sysmsg(5019, account.path) ;* Unable to change to directory %1
   goto revert.to.old.account
end

openpath "voc" to new.voc else
   server.error = SV$ERROR
   error.msg = sysmsg(5163) ;* Directory is not a SD account
   goto revert.to.old.account
end

i = ospath("", os$flush.cache)

account.path = ospath("", os$cwd)     ;* Ensure @PATH is absolute path
initial.account.path = account.path   ;* Make WHO show only one element
who = new.account

voc = new.voc

* 0452 Set up the private catalogue pathname

private.catalogue = 'cat'
read voc.rec from voc, "$PRIVATE.CATALOGUE" then
   if upcase(voc.rec[1,1]) = 'X' then private.catalogue = voc.rec<2>
end

i = kernel(K$PRIVATE.CATALOGUE, private.catalogue)

* Run the LOGIN paragraph, if it exists

* 18 Aug 26 Windows port - AS TYPED, THEN LOWER, PROJECT_STATUS.md 5.12 (b).
*   @voc is a DYNAMIC file, so this is an exact byte match; without the second
*   attempt an API session would silently stop running the LOGIN paragraph the
*   moment the VOC id moves.  Blocked THEN/ELSE deliberately - see 5.12 trap 3.
readv i from @voc, 'LOGIN', 0 on error null
then
   execute 'LOGIN' trapping aborts capturing response
end else
   readv i from @voc, 'login', 0 on error null
   then
      execute 'login' trapping aborts capturing response
   end
end

return

revert.to.old.account:
if not(ospath(old.account.path, OS$CD)) then
   server.error = SV$ERROR
   error.msg = sysmsg(5162) ;* Fatal error : Cannot return to previous account
   return to abort.vbsrvr
end

* 13 Aug 26 Windows port - put @PATH back with the directory.  This restored
*   the one and not the other, so a refused account switch left @PATH holding
*   the path it had failed to reach.

account.path = old.account.path

return

* ======================================================================
* Open file
* In:  fname
* Out: fileno (short integer)

vb.open:
if kernel(K$SDNET, -1)  or config("SDCLIENT") # 0 then
   abort.message = sysmsg(5262) ;* File access is disabled
   server.error = SV$ON.ERROR
   return
end

* Locate a spare file table entry

n = inmat(files)

for i = 1 to n
   if not(fileinfo(files(i), FL$OPEN)) then goto vb.open.continue
next i

* Extend file table

dim files(n + 50)
i = n + 1

vb.open.continue:
* Open file to file table entry i

open cmnd to files(i)
on error server.error = SV$ON.ERROR
then
   if bitand(fileinfo(files(i), FL$FLAGS), FL$FLAGS.TRUSTED) then
      server.error = SV$ELSE
      end else
         response = iconv(i, 'ISL')
      end
   end
   else server.error = SV$ELSE

      return

      * ======================================================================
      * Close file
      * In:  fileno (short integer)
      * Out:

vb.close:
      fno = oconv(cmnd[1,2], 'ISL')
      gosub check.file
      if err then return

      close files(fno)   ;* 0346

      return

      * ======================================================================
      * Read record
      * In:  fileno (short integer)
      *      id
      * Out: record

vb.read:
      fno = oconv(cmnd[1,2], 'ISL')
      gosub check.file
      if err then return

      id = cmnd[3,99]
      read rec from files(fno), id
      on error
      server.error = SV$ON.ERROR
   end then
      response = rec
   end else
      server.error = SV$ELSE
      end

      return

      * ======================================================================
      * Read record with shared lock
      * In:  fileno (short integer)
      *      id
      * Out: record

vb.readl:
      fno = oconv(cmnd[1,2], 'ISL')
      gosub check.file
      if err then return

      id = cmnd[3,99]
      readl rec from files(fno), id
      on error
      server.error = SV$ON.ERROR
   end locked
      server.error = SV$LOCKED
      end then
         response = rec
      end else
         server.error = SV$ELSE
         end

         return

         * ======================================================================
         * Read record with shared lock, waiting if locked
         * In:  fileno (short integer)
         *      id
         * Out: record

vb.readlw:
         fno = oconv(cmnd[1,2], 'ISL')
         gosub check.file
         if err then return

         id = cmnd[3,99]
         readl rec from files(fno), id
         on error
         server.error = SV$ON.ERROR
      end then
         response = rec
      end else
         server.error = SV$ELSE
         end

         return

         * ======================================================================
         * Read record with exclusive lock
         * In:  fileno (short integer)
         *      id
         * Out: record

vb.readu:
         fno = oconv(cmnd[1,2], 'ISL')
         gosub check.file
         if err then return

         id = cmnd[3,99]
         readu rec from files(fno), id
         on error
         server.error = SV$ON.ERROR
      end locked
         server.error = SV$LOCKED
         end then
            response = rec
         end else
            server.error = SV$ELSE
            end

            return

            * ======================================================================
            * Read record with exclusive lock, waiting if locked
            * In:  fileno (short integer)
            *      id
            * Out: record

vb.readuw:
            fno = oconv(cmnd[1,2], 'ISL')
            gosub check.file
            if err then return

            id = cmnd[3,99]
            readu rec from files(fno), id
            on error
            server.error = SV$ON.ERROR
         end then
            response = rec
         end else
            server.error = SV$ELSE
            end

            return

            * ======================================================================
            * Select file
            * In:  file no  (short int)
            *      list no  (short int)

vb.select:
            fno = oconv(cmnd[1,2], 'ISL')
            gosub check.file
            if err then return

            listno = oconv(cmnd[3,2], 'ISL')
            gosub check.list
            if err then return

            select files(fno) to listno

            return

            * ======================================================================
            * Read next entry from select list
            * In:  listno (short integer)
            * Out: id

vb.readnext:
            listno = oconv(cmnd[1,2], 'ISL')
            gosub check.list
            if err then return

            readnext response from listno else server.error = SV$ELSE

               return

               * ======================================================================
               * Clear select list
               * In:  listno (short integer)

vb.clearselect:
               listno = oconv(cmnd[1,2], 'ISL')
               gosub check.list
               if err then return

               clearselect listno

               return

               * ======================================================================
               * Read select list
               * In:  listno (short integer)

vb.readlist:
               listno = oconv(cmnd[1,2], 'ISL')
               gosub check.list
               if err then return

               readlist response from listno else response = ''

               return

               * ======================================================================
               * Release lock
               * In:  fileno (short integer)
               *      id

vb.release:
               fno = oconv(cmnd[1,2], 'ISL')
               if fno then               ;* 0249
                  gosub check.file
                  if err then return
               end

               id = cmnd[3,99]

               begin case
                  case fno = 0
                     release

                  case id = ''
                     release files(fno)

                  case 1
                     release files(fno), id
               end case

               return

               * ======================================================================
               * Write record
               * In:  fileno (short integer)
               *      id_len (short integer)
               *      id
               *      data

vb.write:
               fno = oconv(cmnd[1,2], 'ISL')
               gosub check.file
               if err then return

               id.len = oconv(cmnd[3,2], 'ISL')
               id = cmnd[5,id.len]

               write cmnd[5 + id.len, 99999999] to files(fno), id
               on error server.error = SV$ON.ERROR

               return

               * ======================================================================
               * Write record, retaiining lock
               * In:  fileno (short integer)
               *      id_len (short integer)
               *      id
               *      data

vb.writeu:
               fno = oconv(cmnd[1,2], 'ISL')
               gosub check.file
               if err then return

               id.len = oconv(cmnd[3,2], 'ISL')
               id = cmnd[5,id.len]

               writeu cmnd[5 + id.len, 99999999] to files(fno), id
               on error server.error = SV$ON.ERROR

               return

               * ======================================================================
               * Delete record
               * In:  fileno (short integer)
               *      id

vb.delete:
               fno = oconv(cmnd[1,2], 'ISL')
               gosub check.file
               if err then return

               id = cmnd[3,99]
               delete files(fno), id
               on error server.error = SV$ON.ERROR

               return

               * ======================================================================
               * Delete record, retaining lock
               * In:  fileno (short integer)
               *      id

vb.deleteu:
               fno = oconv(cmnd[1,2], 'ISL')
               gosub check.file
               if err then return

               id = cmnd[3,99]

               deleteu files(fno), id
               on error server.error = SV$ON.ERROR

               return

               * ======================================================================
               * Call catalogued subroutine
               * In:  subr name len (short integer)
               *      subr name (rounded to 2 byte boundary)
               *      arg count (short integer)
               *      arg len (long integer)
               *      arg data (rounded to 2 byte boundary)
               *
               * Out: arg no (short integer)   Always in ascending arg no order
               *      arg len (long integer)
               *      arg data (rounded to 2 byte boundary)

vb.call:
               name.len = oconv(cmnd[1,2], 'ISL')
               if name.len < 1 or name.len > MAX.CALL.NAME.LEN then
                  abort.message = sysmsg(5263) ;* Invalid call name
                  server.error = SV$ON.ERROR
                  return
               end

               subr.name = cmnd[3,name.len]
               pos = 3 + name.len + bitand(name.len, 1)

               arg.count = oconv(cmnd[pos,2], 'ISL')
               pos += 2

               * Are we allowed to run this program?

               obj.flags = load.object(subr.name)
               if subr.name[1,1] = '$' or config("SDCLIENT") = 2 or kernel(K$SDNET, -1) then
                  if not(bitand(obj.flags, HDR.SDCALL.ALLOWED)) then
                     abort.message = sysmsg(5264, subr.name) ;* %1 cannot be called from a SDClient session
                     server.error = SV$ON.ERROR
                  end
               end

               if arg.count then
                  mat args = ''
                  for i = 1 to arg.count
                     arg.len = oconv(cmnd[pos,4], 'ILL')
                     pos += 4
                     args(i) = cmnd[pos,arg.len]
                     pos += arg.len + bitand(arg.len, 1)
                  next i

                  callv @subr.name, arg.count, args

                  * Now return values of changed arguments (if any)

                  for i = 1 to arg.count
                     if changed(args(i)) then
                        response := iconv(i, 'ISL') : iconv(len(args(i)), 'ILL') : args(i)
                        if bitand(len(args(i)), 1) then response := ' '
                     end
                  next i
               end else
                  call @subr.name
               end

               gosub reset.environment

               return

               * ======================================================================
               * Execute command
               * In:  Command string
               * Out: Command output

vb.execute:
               if config("SDCLIENT") # 0  or kernel(K$SDNET, -1) then
                  abort.message = sysmsg(5265) ;* Command execution is disabled
                  server.error = SV$ON.ERROR
                  return
               end

               execute cmnd capturing response
               st = @system.return.code
               return to return.status.set

               * ======================================================================
               * Response to input
               * In:  Command string
               * Should never happen as client end should detect this

vb.respond:
               server.error = SV$ERROR
               error.msg = sysmsg(5266) ;* Response to prompt sent when no prompt outstanding
               return

               * ======================================================================
               * End command
               * Should never happen as client end should detect this

vb.endcommand:
               server.error = SV$ERROR
               error.msg = sysmsg(5267) ;* End command request sent when no prompt outstanding
               return

               * ======================================================================
               * Network login, request 24 - RETIRED.  docs/SCRAM_AUTH.md phase 5.
               *
               * THE CLEARTEXT LOGIN IS GONE AND THERE IS NO FALLBACK.  This
               * handler read a length-prefixed user name and password out of
               * the packet body and passed them to !CRED_VERIFY.  The password
               * crossed the wire in clear, which is the whole reason SCRAM was
               * written; requests 47 and 48 replace it and a client that still
               * sends 24 is refused rather than quietly served a weaker path.
               *
               * IT REFUSES HERE RATHER THAN BEING DROPPED FROM THE GATE ABOVE.
               * Taking 24 out of the "may be sent before authentication" test
               * would answer an old client with 5270 "Not logged in", which is
               * true and useless - it reads as a client bug rather than as a
               * protocol that moved.  One message naming the cause is worth
               * the three lines it costs, and an old client is precisely the
               * caller that will be reading this reply.
               *
               * THE BODY IS NOT PARSED.  It still carries a password, so
               * nothing here reads it, copies it or lets it reach a variable.
               *
               * The connection is dropped, as it was for a failed login.

vb.login:
               abort.message = sysmsg(5275) ;* Request no longer supported...
               server.error = SV$ON.ERROR
               done = @true

               return

               * ======================================================================
               * Login user for SDLocal connection

vb.local.login:
              * dsm 20240612 openpath @sdsys:@ds:'$LOGINS' to lgn.f else
              * dsm 20240612    abort.message = sysmsg(6050) ;* Cannot open $LOGINS register
              * dsm 20240612    server.error = SV$ON.ERROR
              * dsm 20240612    return
              * dsm 20240612 end

               * mab 20240219  read security.rec from lgn.f, '$SECURE' then
               * mab 20240219     = kernel(K$SECURE, security.rec<1>)
               * mab 20240219  end

               username = logname

               * mab 20240219 if kernel(K$SECURE, -1) then
               * dsm 20240612 readu lgn.rec from lgn.f, username else null
               * 20240219 mab user must be member of sdusers           
* 13 Aug 26 Windows port - removed the sdusers group test; SD no longer
*   consults operating system groups.

               * dsm 20240612 lgn.rec<LGN$DATE> = date()
               * dsm 20240612 lgn.rec<LGN$TIME> = time()
               * dsm 20240612 recordlocku lgn.f, username
               * dsm 20240612 write lgn.rec to lgn.f, username

               logname = username
               * dsm 20240612 i = kernel(K$ADMINISTRATOR,lgn.rec<LGN$ADMIN>)
               * mab 20240219    end else      ;* System is insecure
               * mab 20240219      i = kernel(K$ADMINISTRATOR,1)    ;* All users are administrators
               * mab 20240219    end

exit.vb.local.login:
               * dsm 20240612close lgn.f
               if server.error = SV$OK then logged.in = @true
               else done = @true

               return

               * ======================================================================
               * SCRAM-SHA-256 login, client-first.  docs/SCRAM_AUTH.md, phase 3.
               *
               * In:   n,,n=<user>,r=<client nonce>
               * Out:  r=<combined nonce>,s=<salt>,i=<iterations>
               *
               * NO PASSWORD CROSSES THE WIRE IN EITHER DIRECTION, which is the
               * whole point of replacing request 24.  The server publishes the
               * salt and the cost, the client answers a nonce, and a capture of
               * both packets yields an offline guess bounded by the iteration
               * count and nothing else.
               *
               * THE BODY IS THE SCRAM MESSAGE AND NOTHING ELSE.  vb.login's body
               * is length-prefixed fields each padded to a two byte multiple;
               * this one is not, because the packet is already length delimited.
               * scram.trim.body drops trailing NULs anyway - see there for why.
               *
               * THE SERVER DOES NOT RUN PBKDF2 HERE.  It holds StoredKey, so
               * the 600,000 iterations are spent once, in SET.PASSWORD.  Login
               * costs two HMACs and a hash, which is what makes it safe to do
               * this work before the client has proved anything.

vb.scram.first:
               gosub scram.trim.body

               * A fresh exchange on a session that has already authenticated is
               * a client bug or an attempt to change identity part way through.
               * vb.login needed no such guard because it was a single message
               * that set logged.in and nothing followed it.
               if logged.in then
                  abort.message = sysmsg(5273) ;* Authentication sequence error
                  server.error = SV$ON.ERROR
                  goto exit.vb.scram.fail
               end

               scram.stage = 0        ;* a restart abandons any exchange in flight

               * GS2 header.  'n,,' is "no channel binding", and it is honest -
               * there is no TLS channel here to bind to.  'y,,' claims the
               * server does not support binding, which is the downgrade signal,
               * and 'p=' demands a binding that does not exist.  Both refused.
               if cmnd[1,3] # 'n,,' then goto scram.bad.message

               scram.cfirst.bare = cmnd[4,99999999]

               * Exactly two attributes.  RFC 5802 section 5 requires the server
               * to FAIL on an m= mandatory extension rather than ignore it, and
               * counting the commas is what makes that automatic: anything
               * extra, in any position, lands here.
               *
               * It also settles the nonce.  A client nonce containing a comma
               * would split into three fields and be refused now, rather than
               * mismatching later for reasons nobody could see.
               if count(scram.cfirst.bare, ',') # 1 then goto scram.bad.message

               scram.attr = field(scram.cfirst.bare, ',', 1)
               if scram.attr[1,2] # 'n=' then goto scram.bad.message
               username = scram.attr[3,99999999]

               scram.attr = field(scram.cfirst.bare, ',', 2)
               if scram.attr[1,2] # 'r=' then goto scram.bad.message
               scram.cnonce = scram.attr[3,99999999]
               if scram.cnonce = '' then goto scram.bad.message

               * NO =2C / =3D UNESCAPING, and none is needed: valid_os_name
               * allows letters, digits, dot, underscore and hyphen only, so a
               * name that would have required escaping cannot be a user here.
               * Refusing it is therefore the same answer as decoding it.
               if username = '' or username[1,1] = '$' then goto scram.bad.cred
               if not(valid_os_name(username)) then goto scram.bad.cred

               openpath @sdsys:@ds:'$cred' to scram.cred.f else
                  abort.message = sysmsg(5274) ;* Authentication service unavailable
                  server.error = SV$ON.ERROR
                  goto exit.vb.scram.fail
               end

               read scram.cred from scram.cred.f, upcase(username) else
                  close scram.cred.f
                  goto scram.bad.cred      ;* no credential - fail closed
               end
               close scram.cred.f

               * A version 1 record holds an Argon2 verifier and no StoredKey.
               * It cannot drive a SCRAM exchange and cannot be converted - the
               * plaintext was never stored, by design - so the account has to
               * run SET.PASSWORD again.  !CRED_VERIFY refuses it the same way.
               if scram.cred<CRED$VERSION> # SCRAM$CRED.VERSION then
                  scram.cred = ''
                  goto scram.bad.cred
               end

               scram.salt = scram.cred<CRED$SALT>
               scram.iter = scram.cred<CRED$ITER>
               scram.storedkey = scram.cred<CRED$STOREDKEY>
               scram.serverkey = scram.cred<CRED$SERVERKEY>
               scram.cred = ''

               if scram.salt = '' or scram.iter = '' then goto scram.bad.cred
               if scram.storedkey = '' or scram.serverkey = '' then goto scram.bad.cred

               * 18 RANDOM BYTES, AND THE 18 IS NOT ARBITRARY.  It is a multiple
               * of three, so base64 encodes it with no '=' padding, and every
               * character base64 emits is inside RFC 5802's printable set -
               * which excludes the comma this message is parsed on and the
               * space that would end it.
               scram.snonce = SDEXT('18', @TRUE, SD_RANDBYTES)
               if scram.snonce = '' then goto scram.crypto.failed

               scram.nonce = scram.cnonce : scram.snonce

               * KEPT VERBATIM, NOT REBUILT.  server-first goes into AuthMessage
               * byte for byte, so storing the string that was actually sent
               * removes any chance of the two differing - which would fail the
               * signature check with nothing to show for it.
               scram.sfirst = 'r=' : scram.nonce : ',s=' : scram.salt : ',i=' : scram.iter

               scram.user = username
               scram.stage = 1
               response = scram.sfirst

               return

               * ======================================================================
               * SCRAM-SHA-256 login, client-final.  docs/SCRAM_AUTH.md, phase 3.
               *
               * In:   c=biws,r=<combined nonce>,p=<ClientProof>
               * Out:  v=<ServerSignature>
               *
               * THE SERVER NEVER HOLDS ClientKey.  It recovers a candidate from
               * the proof and checks its SHA-256 against StoredKey, so a stolen
               * $cred still cannot authenticate as the client - forming a proof
               * needs the preimage.  It CAN impersonate the server, which is
               * why the $cred ACL matters exactly as much as it did before.

vb.scram.final:
               gosub scram.trim.body

               if logged.in then
                  abort.message = sysmsg(5273) ;* Authentication sequence error
                  server.error = SV$ON.ERROR
                  goto exit.vb.scram.fail
               end

               * A client-final with no client-first before it has no nonce to
               * answer and no AuthMessage to sign.  Refusing here is the point:
               * running the comparison against empty values is the shape of bug
               * that turns a signature check into a formality.
               if scram.stage # 1 then
                  abort.message = sysmsg(5273) ;* Authentication sequence error
                  server.error = SV$ON.ERROR
                  goto exit.vb.scram.fail
               end

               * ONE ATTEMPT PER CLIENT-FIRST.  Cleared before the proof is
               * examined, so a client cannot sit on one server-first and grind
               * proofs against it - each guess costs a fresh round trip and the
               * three second sleep below.
               scram.stage = 0

               if count(cmnd, ',') # 2 then goto scram.bad.message

               * 'biws' is base64("n,,") - the header the exchange began with,
               * echoed back so it cannot be stripped in flight.  It is a literal
               * because the only header accepted at 47 was a literal.
               scram.attr = field(cmnd, ',', 1)
               if scram.attr # 'c=biws' then goto scram.bad.message

               scram.attr = field(cmnd, ',', 2)
               if scram.attr[1,2] # 'r=' then goto scram.bad.message

               * EXACT MATCH ON THE WHOLE COMBINED NONCE.  This is what kills
               * replay: the server half was generated for this exchange and for
               * no other, so a client-final captured earlier answers a nonce
               * that no longer exists.
               if scram.attr[3,99999999] # scram.nonce then goto scram.bad.message

               scram.cfinal.bare = 'c=biws,' : scram.attr

               scram.attr = field(cmnd, ',', 3)
               if scram.attr[1,2] # 'p=' then goto scram.bad.message
               scram.proof = scram.attr[3,99999999]
               if scram.proof = '' then goto scram.bad.message

               scram.authmsg = scram.cfirst.bare : ',' : scram.sfirst : ',' : scram.cfinal.bare

               * EVERY FAILURE FROM HERE ON IS ONE ANSWER.  The nonce matched,
               * so the caller is talking about a real exchange; whether the
               * proof was malformed, the wrong length or simply wrong is its
               * own business and telling it apart helps nobody but a guesser.
               scram.csig = SDEXT(scram.storedkey : @FM : scram.authmsg, @TRUE, SD_HMACSHA256)
               if scram.csig = '' then goto scram.crypto.failed

               scram.ckey = SDEXT(scram.proof : @FM : scram.csig, @TRUE, SD_XORBYTES)
               if scram.ckey = '' then goto scram.bad.cred

               scram.derived = SDEXT(scram.ckey, @TRUE, SD_SHA256)
               scram.ckey = ''
               if scram.derived = '' then goto scram.bad.cred

               * Constant time, as !CRED_VERIFY is.  The primitive was written
               * for this call as much as for that one.
               if SDEXT(scram.derived : @FM : scram.storedkey, @TRUE, SD_CTEQUAL) # '1' then
                  goto scram.bad.cred
               end

               * AUTHENTICATED.  The reply is a signature only a holder of this
               * account's ServerKey can compute, and that is the mutual half:
               * a process that took the port before SD started can collect a
               * proof it cannot use, but cannot produce this, so the client
               * detects it.  A client that treats a missing or wrong v= as a
               * warning throws that away - see docs/SCRAM_AUTH.md, phase 4.
               scram.ssig = SDEXT(scram.serverkey : @FM : scram.authmsg, @TRUE, SD_HMACSHA256)
               if scram.ssig = '' then goto scram.crypto.failed

               * THE IDENTITY IS THE NAME THAT WAS PROVEN, UNCONDITIONALLY.
               * vb.login consulted config('APILOGIN') here and, when it was 0,
               * discarded the supplied name in favour of kernel(K$USERNAME) -
               * "the peer authenticated over the tunnel already".  That branch
               * rested on getpeereid(), which Windows has no equivalent of and
               * which op_kernel.c records as gone; peer_usr_id is deliberately
               * left unassigned, PROJECT_STATUS.md section 7 step 6.  There is
               * no unauthenticated SCRAM in any case - the exchange cannot
               * start without a user name and cannot finish without proof of
               * its password - so the config test has nothing left to choose
               * between.  K$SET.USERNAME is refused to a caller that is not
               * $internal; this program is.
               logname = scram.user
               void kernel(K$SET.USERNAME, scram.user)

               scram.storedkey = ''
               scram.serverkey = ''

               response = 'v=' : scram.ssig
               logged.in = @true

               return

               * ----------------------------------------------------------------------
               * Shared exits for both SCRAM handlers.  Reached by goto from either;
               * each ends in the return that leaves the handler.

scram.bad.message:
               abort.message = sysmsg(5272) ;* Invalid authentication message
               server.error = SV$ON.ERROR
               goto exit.vb.scram.fail

scram.crypto.failed:
               * A primitive that fails is a fault in this server, not a wrong
               * password, and saying so costs nothing: it tells an attacker
               * only that SDEXT is broken, which no credential depends on.
               abort.message = sysmsg(5274) ;* Authentication service unavailable
               server.error = SV$ON.ERROR
               goto exit.vb.scram.fail

scram.bad.cred:
               * ONE MESSAGE AND ONE DELAY FOR EVERY CREDENTIAL FAILURE, as
               * vb.login has.  Unknown account, version 1 record and wrong
               * password read identically in the reply.
               *
               * THEY ARE NOT IDENTICAL IN THE ROUND TRIP, and that is a known
               * gap rather than an oversight: an account with no usable
               * credential fails at 47, a wrong password at 48, so the two are
               * distinguishable by which request was refused.  RFC 5802's
               * answer is a dummy salt derived from a server-held secret, so an
               * unknown account receives a plausible server-first and fails at
               * 48 like everyone else.  That needs a secret this program can
               * read but not write - docs/SCRAM_AUTH.md, "Still open".
               abort.message = sysmsg(5017) ;* Invalid username or password
               server.error = SV$ON.ERROR
               sleep 3
               goto exit.vb.scram.fail

exit.vb.scram.fail:
               * THE CONNECTION GOES, as it does for a failed request 24.  It is
               * also the only brake besides the sleep: there is still no
               * lockout, so making each guess pay for a new connection is worth
               * the little it buys.
               scram.stage = 0
               scram.storedkey = ''
               scram.serverkey = ''
               done = @true

               return

               * ----------------------------------------------------------------------
               * Drop trailing NULs from the request body.
               *
               * THE MESSAGE NEEDS NO PADDING AND MUST NOT BE GIVEN ANY - the
               * packet carries its own length.  But vb.login's body pads every
               * field to a two byte multiple with a NUL, and a client written
               * from that precedent would put one inside the base64, where it
               * would surface as "authentication failed" with nothing to show
               * which byte was at fault.  NUL is not valid anywhere in a SCRAM
               * message, so dropping it here can only remove padding.

scram.trim.body:
               loop
               while cmnd # '' and cmnd[len(cmnd),1] = char(0)
                  cmnd = cmnd[1,len(cmnd)-1]
               repeat

               return

               * ======================================================================
               * Select index
               * In:  file no  (short int)
               *      list no  (short int)
               *      index name len (short int)
               *      index name (padded to 2 byte interval)
               *      index value len (short int)
               *      index value (padded to 2 byte interval)

vb.selectindex:
               fno = oconv(cmnd[1,2], 'ISL')
               gosub check.file
               if err then return

               listno = oconv(cmnd[3,2], 'ISL')
               gosub check.list
               if err then return

               * Extract index name

               pos = 5
               n = oconv(cmnd[pos,2], 'ISL')
               pos += 2
               index.name = cmnd[pos, n]
               pos += n + bitand(n, 1)

               * Extract index value

               n = oconv(cmnd[pos,2], 'ISL')
               pos += 2
               index.value = cmnd[pos, n]

               selectindex index.name, index.value from files(fno) to listno

               return

                     * ======================================================================
                     * Open file SDNet file
                     * In:  Account name;filename
                     * Out: fileno (short integer)

vb.open.sdnet:
                     if not(bitand(config('NETFILES'), 2)) then
                        set.status ER$XREMOTE
                        server.error = SV$ELSE
                           return
                        end

                        * Use of this operation identifies the process as a SDNet user.
                        * Set the appropriate process flag so that LISTU etc show this.

                        i = kernel(K$SDNET, 1)

                        * Locate a spare file table entry

                        n = inmat(files)

                        for i = 1 to n
                           if not(fileinfo(files(i), FL$OPEN)) then goto vb.open.sdnet.continue
                        next i

                        * Extend file table

                        dim files(n + 50)
                        i = n + 1

vb.open.sdnet.continue:

                        * Open file to file table entry i

                        acc = field(cmnd, ';', 1)   ;* Account name or path
                        file = field(cmnd, ';', 1)  ;* File name

                        openpath @sdsys:@ds:'accounts' to acc.f then
                           read acc.rec from acc.f, acc then
                              acc = parse.pathname.tokens(acc.rec<ACC$PATH>)
                           end
                           close acc.f
                        end

                        qvoc.path = acc:@ds:'voc'
                        openpath qvoc.path to qvoc.f else
                           server.error = SV$ELSE
                              return
                           end

                           file = field(cmnd, ';', 2)
                           if file[1,5] = 'DICT ' then
                              j = 3
                              file = file[6,999]
                           end else
                              j = 2
                           end

                           read voc.rec from qvoc.f, file else null
                           close qvoc.f

                           if voc.rec[1,1] # 'F' then
                              set.status ER$VNF
                              server.error = SV$ELSE
                                 return
                              end

                              path = voc.rec<j>
                              if path = '' then
                                 set.status ER$NPN
                                 server.error = SV$ELSE
                                    return
                                 end

                                 if upcase(path[1,6]) = '@SDSYS' then path = @sdsys:path[7,9999]

                                 if path[1,1] # @ds then
                                    * Convert voc item to absolute path
                                    path = acc : @ds : path
                                 end

                                 openpath path to files(i)
                                 on error server.error = SV$ON.ERROR
                                 then
                                    if bitand(fileinfo(files(i), FL$FLAGS), FL$FLAGS.TRUSTED) then
                                       server.error = SV$ELSE
                                       end else
                                          response = iconv(i, 'ISL')
                                       end
                                    end
                                    else server.error = SV$ELSE

                                       return

                                       * ======================================================================
                                       * Lock record
                                       * In:  fileno (short integer)
                                       *      flags (short integer)    0x0001 = Update lock, 0x0002 = no wait.
                                       *      id

vb.lock.record:
                                       fno = oconv(cmnd[1,2], 'ISL')
                                       gosub check.file
                                       if err then return

                                       flags = oconv(cmnd[3,2], 'ISL')

                                       id = cmnd[5,99]

                                       begin case
                                          case flags = 0
                                             recordlockl files(fno), id
                                          case flags = 1
                                             recordlocku files(fno), id
                                          case flags = 2
                                             recordlockl files(fno), id locked server.error = SV$LOCKED
                                             case flags = 3
                                                recordlocku files(fno), id locked server.error = SV$LOCKED
                                             end case

                                             return

                                             * ======================================================================
                                             * Clear file
                                             * In:  fileno (short integer)
                                             * Out:

vb.clearfile:
                                             fno = oconv(cmnd[1,2], 'ISL')
                                             gosub check.file
                                             if err then return

                                             clearfile files(i)

                                             return

                                             * ======================================================================
                                             * Get file lock
                                             * In:  fileno (short integer)
                                             *      Wait?  (short integer)
                                             * Out:

vb.filelock:
                                             fno = oconv(cmnd[1,2], 'ISL')
                                             wait = oconv(cmnd[3,2], 'ISL')
                                             gosub check.file
                                             if err then return

                                             if wait then
                                                filelock files(i)
                                             end else
                                                filelock files(i) locked server.error = SV$LOCKED
                                                end

                                                return

                                                * ======================================================================
                                                * Release file lock
                                                * In:  fileno (short integer)
                                                * Out:

vb.fileunlock:
                                                fno = oconv(cmnd[1,2], 'ISL')
                                                gosub check.file
                                                if err then return

                                                fileunlock files(i)

                                                return

                                                * ======================================================================
                                                * Test lock
                                                * In:  fileno (short integer)
                                                *      id

vb.recordlocked:
                                                fno = oconv(cmnd[1,2], 'ISL')
                                                gosub check.file
                                                if err then return

                                                id = cmnd[3,99]
                                                i = recordlocked(files(fno), id)
                                                st = status()
                                                response = iconv(i, 'ILL');
                                                set.status st

                                                return

                                                * ======================================================================
                                                * Fetch information about indices
                                                * In:  fileno (short integer)

vb.indices1:
                                                fno = oconv(cmnd[1,2], 'ISL')
                                                gosub check.file
                                                if err then return

                                                response = indices(files(fno))

                                                return

                                                * ======================================================================
                                                * Fetch information about indices
                                                * In:  fileno (short integer)
                                                *      Index name

vb.indices2:
                                                fno = oconv(cmnd[1,2], 'ISL')
                                                gosub check.file
                                                if err then return

                                                response = indices(files(fno), cmnd[3,99])

                                                return

                                                * ======================================================================
                                                * Select file and return list
                                                * In:  fileno (short integer)

vb.selectlist:
                                                fno = oconv(cmnd[1,2], 'ISL')
                                                gosub check.file
                                                if err then return

                                                select files(fno) to 11
                                                readlist response from 11 else null

                                                return

                                                * ======================================================================
                                                * Select index, returning indexed values
                                                * In:  fileno (short integer)
                                                *      index name

vb.selectindexv:
                                                fno = oconv(cmnd[1,2], 'ISL')
                                                gosub check.file
                                                if err then return

                                                index.name = cmnd[3,999]
                                                selectindex cmnd[3,99] from files(fno) to 11
                                                readlist response from 11 else null

                                                return

                                                * ======================================================================
                                                * Select index, returning keys for indexed value
                                                * In:  fileno (short integer)
                                                *      index name len (short integer)
                                                *      index name
                                                *      indexed value

vb.selectindexk:
                                                fno = oconv(cmnd[1,2], 'ISL')
                                                gosub check.file
                                                if err then return

                                                i = oconv(cmnd[3,2], 'ISL')
                                                index.name = cmnd[5,i]

                                                selectindex index.name, cmnd[5+i,999] from files(fno) to 11
                                                readlist response from 11 else null

                                                return

                                                * ======================================================================
                                                * Perform FILEINFO() action
                                                * In:  fileno (short integer)
                                                *      key (long integer)

vb.fileinfo:
                                                fno = oconv(cmnd[1,2], 'ISL')
                                                gosub check.file
                                                if err then return

                                                i = oconv(cmnd[3,4], 'ILL')
                                                response = fileinfo(files(fno), i)

                                                return

                                                * ======================================================================
                                                * READV and variants
                                                * In:  fileno (short integer)
                                                *      flags  (short integer) 1 = update lock, 2 = shared lock, 4 = no wait
                                                *      field no (long integer)
                                                *      id
                                                * Out: record data

vb.readv:
                                                fno = oconv(cmnd[1,2], 'ISL')
                                                gosub check.file
                                                if err then return

                                                flags = oconv(cmnd[3,2], 'ISL')
                                                field_no = oconv(cmnd[5,4], 'ILL')

                                                id = cmnd[9,99]

                                                begin case
                                                   case flags = 0
                                                      readv rec from files(fno), id, field_no
                                                      on error server.error = SV$ON.ERROR
                                                      then response = rec
                                                      else server.error = SV$ELSE

                                                      case flags = 1
                                                         readvu rec from files(fno), id, field_no
                                                         on error server.error = SV$ON.ERROR
                                                         then response = rec
                                                         else server.error = SV$ELSE

                                                         case flags = 2
                                                            readvl rec from files(fno), id, field_no
                                                            on error server.error = SV$ON.ERROR
                                                            then response = rec
                                                            else server.error = SV$ELSE

                                                            case flags = 5
                                                               readvu rec from files(fno), id, field_no
                                                               on error server.error = SV$ON.ERROR
                                                               locked server.error = SV$LOCKED
                                                                  then response = rec
                                                                  else server.error = SV$ELSE

                                                                  case flags = 6
                                                                     readvl rec from files(fno), id, field_no
                                                                     on error server.error = SV$ON.ERROR
                                                                     locked server.error = SV$LOCKED
                                                                        then response = rec
                                                                        else server.error = SV$ELSE
                                                                     end case

                                                                     return

                                                                     * ======================================================================
                                                                     * SetLeft
                                                                     * In:  fileno (short integer)
                                                                     *      index name

vb.setleft:
                                                                     fno = oconv(cmnd[1,2], 'ISL')
                                                                     gosub check.file
                                                                     if err then return

                                                                     setleft cmnd[3,999] from files(fno)

                                                                     return

                                                                     * ======================================================================
                                                                     * SetRight
                                                                     * In:  fileno (short integer)
                                                                     *      index name

vb.setright:
                                                                     fno = oconv(cmnd[1,2], 'ISL')
                                                                     gosub check.file
                                                                     if err then return

                                                                     setright cmnd[3,999] from files(fno)

                                                                     return

                                                                     * ======================================================================
                                                                     * SelectLeft
                                                                     * In:  fileno (short integer)
                                                                     *      list no (short integer)
                                                                     *      index name

vb.selectleft:
                                                                     fno = oconv(cmnd[1,2], 'ISL')
                                                                     gosub check.file
                                                                     if err then return

                                                                     listno = oconv(cmnd[3,2], 'ISL')

                                                                     selectleft cmnd[5,999] from files(fno) setting response to listno

                                                                     return

                                                                     * ======================================================================
                                                                     * SelectRight
                                                                     * In:  fileno (short integer)
                                                                     *      list no (short integer)
                                                                     *      index name

vb.selectright:
                                                                     fno = oconv(cmnd[1,2], 'ISL')
                                                                     gosub check.file
                                                                     if err then return

                                                                     listno = oconv(cmnd[3,2], 'ISL')

                                                                     selectright cmnd[5,999] from files(fno) setting response to listno

                                                                     * ======================================================================
                                                                     * MarkMapping
                                                                     * In:  fileno (short integer)
                                                                     *      state (short integer)

vb.mark.mapping:
                                                                     fno = oconv(cmnd[1,2], 'ISL')
                                                                     gosub check.file
                                                                     if err then return

                                                                     mark.mapping files(fno), oconv(cmnd[3,2], 'ISL')

                                                                     return

                                                                     * ======================================================================
check.file:
                                                                     err = @true

                                                                     if fno < 1 or fno > inmat(files) then      ;* Invalid file number
                                                                        server.error = SV$ERROR
                                                                        error.msg = sysmsg(5268) ;* Invalid file number
                                                                        return
                                                                     end

                                                                     if not(fileinfo(files(fno), FL$OPEN)) then ;* File not open
                                                                        server.error = SV$ERROR
                                                                        error.msg = sysmsg(5268) ;* Invalid file number
                                                                        return
                                                                     end

                                                                     err = @false
                                                                     return


                                                                     * ======================================================================
check.list:
                                                                     err = @true

                                                                     if listno < 0 or listno > 10 then      ;* Invalid list number   0225
                                                                        server.error = SV$ERROR
                                                                        error.msg = sysmsg(5269) ;* Invalid select list number
                                                                        return
                                                                     end

                                                                     err = @false
                                                                     return
                                                                  end



